@page "/home"

<div class="container py-4">
    <div class="border rounded p-3 mb-4 bg-dark text-white">
        <div class="row align-items-center g-3">
            <div class="col-12 col-md-3 text-center">
                <img src="icon-192.png" alt="VGS Texture Packer cover" class="img-fluid rounded" style="max-width: 180px;" />
            </div>
            <div class="col-12 col-md-9">
                <h2 class="mb-2">Texture Workflow Hub</h2>
                <p class="mb-0">
                    Use this workspace to convert textures, generate maps, and package ORMs with a consistent pipeline.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mb-4">
        <h1 class="mb-2">VGS Texture Packer</h1>
        <p class="lead mb-0">
            Workspace for creating PBR maps, building ORM textures, and exporting assets to different formats.
            From here you can access every tool and follow a recommended workflow.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="row g-3 mb-4">
        <div class="col-12 col-md-6 col-xl-4">
            <div class="border rounded p-3 h-100">
                <h4>Create ORMs by File</h4>
                <p class="mb-3">Load 3 maps (AO, Roughness, and Metallic/Gloss) and generate a single ORM texture.</p>
                <a class="btn btn-primary" href="autoarchivo">Go to Create ORM Image</a>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="col-12 col-md-6 col-xl-4">
            <div class="border rounded p-3 h-100">
                <h4>Create ORMs by Folder</h4>
                <p class="mb-3">Select a full folder to detect groups automatically and generate ORM textures in batch.</p>
                <a class="btn btn-primary" href="autocarpeta">Go to Create ORM Folder</a>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="col-12 col-md-6 col-xl-4">
            <div class="border rounded p-3 h-100">
                <h4>Generate Maps from Diffuse</h4>
                <p class="mb-3">Start from a base texture and generate AO, Roughness, Metallic/Gloss, and Normal using adjustable parameters.</p>
                <a class="btn btn-primary" href="crearmapas">Go to Create Maps</a>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="col-12 col-md-6 col-xl-4">
            <div class="border rounded p-3 h-100">
                <h4>Generate Maps by Folder</h4>
                <p class="mb-3">Process many diffuse textures at once and create AO, Roughness, Gloss, and Normal maps in an output folder.</p>
                <a class="btn btn-primary" href="crearmapascarpeta">Go to Create Maps Folder</a>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="col-12 col-md-6 col-xl-4">
            <div class="border rounded p-3 h-100">
                <h4>Export by Folder</h4>
                <p class="mb-3">Convert all images in a folder to PNG or WebP and save them to a destination folder.</p>
                <a class="btn btn-primary" href="exportarextension">Go to Export Folder</a>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="col-12 col-md-6 col-xl-4">
            <div class="border rounded p-3 h-100">
                <h4>Export by File</h4>
                <p class="mb-3">Convert a single image to PNG or WebP and choose its final destination.</p>
                <a class="btn btn-primary" href="exportarextensionarchivo">Go to Export File</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="border rounded p-4 bg-light">
        <h3 class="mb-3">Recommended Workflow</h3>
        <ol class="mb-0">
            <li class="mb-2">
                If you only have base textures, start in <a href="crearmapas">Create Maps</a> or <a href="crearmapascarpeta">Create Maps Folder</a> to generate AO, Roughness, Metallic/Gloss, and Normal maps.
            </li>
            <li class="mb-2">
                Once the maps are ready, build ORM textures in <a href="autoarchivo">Create ORM Image</a> (single case) or <a href="autocarpeta">Create ORM Folder</a> (larger projects).
            </li>
            <li>
                If you need to standardize formats for your engine or pipeline, finish in <a href="exportarextensionarchivo">Export File</a> or <a href="exportarextension">Export Folder</a>.
            </li>
        </ol>
    </div>
</div>
